\f0\b \cf0 Sir Winston Leonard Spencer Churchill
\f1\b0 ,{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winston_Churchill#cite_note-2"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs25\fsmilli12588 \cf2 \super [a]}}\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knight_of_the_Order_of_the_Garter"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 KG}},\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Member_of_the_Order_of_Merit"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 OM}},\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Companion_of_Honour"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 CH}},\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Territorial_Decoration"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 TD}},\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deputy_Lieutenant"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 DL}},\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fellow_of_the_Royal_Society"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 FRS}},\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Academician"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 RA}}\'a0(30 November 1874\'a0\'96 24 January 1965) was a British statesman who served as\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prime_Minister_of_the_United_Kingdom"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 Prime Minister of the United Kingdom}}\'a0from 1940 to 1945,\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winston_Churchill_in_the_Second_World_War"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 \ul \ulc2 during the Second World War}}, and again from 1951 to 1955. Although best known for his wartime leadership as Prime Minister, Churchill was also a\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Military_Academy,_Sandhurst"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 Sandhurst}}-educated soldier, a\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nobel_Prize_for_Literature"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 Nobel Prize}}-winning\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winston_Churchill_as_a_writer"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 writer}}\'a0and\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winston_Churchill_as_historian"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 historian}}, a prolific\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winston_Churchill_as_painter"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 painter}}, and one of the longest-serving politicians in British history. Apart from two years between 1922 and 1924, he was a\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Member_of_Parliament_(United_Kingdom)"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 Member of Parliament}}\'a0(MP) from 1900 to 1964 and represented a total of five\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UK_Parliament_constituency"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 constituencies}}. Ideologically an\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Economic_liberalism"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 economic liberal}}\'a0and\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_Empire"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 imperialist}}, he was for most of his career a member of the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conservative_Party_(UK)"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 Conservative Party}}, which he led from 1940 to 1955, though he was also a member of the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liberal_Party_(UK)"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 Liberal Party}}\'a0from 1904 to 1924.\
\
\
Of mixed English and American parentage, Churchill was born in\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oxfordshire"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 Oxfordshire}}\'a0to\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spencer_family"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 a wealthy, aristocratic family}}. He joined the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_Army"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 British Army}}\'a0in 1895 and saw action in\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_Raj"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 British India}}, the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mahdist_War"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 Anglo-Sudan War}}, and the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Boer_War"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 Second Boer War}}, gaining fame as a\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War_correspondent"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 war correspondent}}\'a0and writing books about his campaigns. Elected a Conservative MP in 1900, he defected to the Liberals in 1904. In\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/H._H._Asquith"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 H. H. Asquith}}'s\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liberal_government,_1905%E2%80%931915"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 Liberal government}}, Churchill served as\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_the_Board_of_Trade"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 President of the Board of Trade}}\'a0and\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Home_Secretary"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 Home Secretary}}, championing\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liberal_welfare_reforms"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 prison reform and workers' social security}}. As\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Lord_of_the_Admiralty"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 First Lord of the Admiralty}}\'a0during the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_World_War"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 First World War}}, he oversaw the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gallipoli_campaign"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 Gallipoli Campaign}}\'a0but, after it proved a disaster, he was demoted to\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chancellor_of_the_Duchy_of_Lancaster"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 Chancellor of the Duchy of Lancaster}}. \

